<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Preparations for proving Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1 (Long-Context Instability). ‣ 2.2 Distance Bias ‣ 2 Theoretical Estimates for Rotary Positional Embedding (RoPE) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>, <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2. ‣ Remark ‣ 2.2 Distance Bias ‣ 2 Theoretical Estimates for Rotary Positional Embedding (RoPE) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>, and <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ Remark ‣ 2.2 Distance Bias ‣ 2 Theoretical Estimates for Rotary Positional Embedding (RoPE) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a></h2>

<div id="A1.Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A1.Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption A.1</span></span><span id="A1.Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{q_{d}^{(m)}\}_{d,m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{q_{d}^{(m)}\}_{d,m}</annotation></semantics></math> (respectively <math id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{k_{d}^{(n)}\}_{d,n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>d</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{k_{d}^{(n)}\}_{d,n}</annotation></semantics></math>) are iids with distribution <math id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{q}</annotation></semantics></math> (respectively <math id="A1.Thmassumption1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>).</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Under Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption A.1. ‣ Appendix A Preparations for proving Theorem , , and ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, the following expectations are constant in <math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d,m,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d,m,n</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A1.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathbb{E}_{q,k}A_{d}^{(m,n)}\equiv\mu_{0},\quad\mathbb{E}_{q,k}B_{d}^{(m,n)}\equiv\nu_{0},\quad\mathbb{E}_{q_{d},k_{d}}|q^{(m)}_{d}k^{(n)}_{d}|^{2}\equiv\sigma_{0}^{2}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi>A</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≡</mo><mi>μ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mi>B</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>≡</mo><mi>ν</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mi>k</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">≡</mo><mi>σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathbb{E}_{q,k}A_{d}^{(m,n)}\equiv\mu_{0},\quad\mathbb{E}_{q,k}B_{d}^{(m,n)}\equiv\nu_{0},\quad\mathbb{E}_{q_{d},k_{d}}|q^{(m)}_{d}k^{(n)}_{d}|^{2}\equiv\sigma_{0}^{2}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the following decomposition of (<a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2.1 Background ‣ 2 Theoretical Estimates for Rotary Positional Embedding (RoPE) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A1.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}\text{Attn}_{\text{RoPE}}(q^{(m)},k^{(n)})=&amp;\bigg(\frac{\mu_{0}}{D}\cdot\sum_{d=0}^{D/2-1}\cos 2\pi(m-n)\theta_{d}+\frac{\nu_{0}}{D}\cdot\sum_{d=0}^{D/2-1}\sin 2\pi(m-n)\theta_{d}\bigg)\\
&amp;+\frac{1}{D}\bigg(\sum_{d=0}^{D/2}(A_{d}-\mu_{0})\cos 2\pi(m-n)\theta_{d}+\sum_{d=0}^{D/2}(B_{d}-\nu_{0})\sin 2\pi(m-n)\theta_{d}\bigg)\\
\eqqcolon&amp;\Gamma_{\lambda}+Z_{\lambda}\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mtext>RoPE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>≕</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\frac{1}{\sqrt{D}}\text{Attn}_{\text{RoPE}}(q^{(m)},k^{(n)})=&amp;\bigg(\frac{\mu_{0}}{D}\cdot\sum_{d=0}^{D/2-1}\cos 2\pi(m-n)\theta_{d}+\frac{\nu_{0}}{D}\cdot\sum_{d=0}^{D/2-1}\sin 2\pi(m-n)\theta_{d}\bigg)\\
&amp;+\frac{1}{D}\bigg(\sum_{d=0}^{D/2}(A_{d}-\mu_{0})\cos 2\pi(m-n)\theta_{d}+\sum_{d=0}^{D/2}(B_{d}-\nu_{0})\sin 2\pi(m-n)\theta_{d}\bigg)\\
\eqqcolon&amp;\Gamma_{\lambda}+Z_{\lambda}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=m-n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=m-n</annotation></semantics></math>. Note that <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{q,k}Z_{\lambda}=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{q,k}Z_{\lambda}=0</annotation></semantics></math> by definition (<a href="#A1.E16" title="In Appendix A Preparations for proving Theorem , , and ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>), and LHS of (<a href="#S2.E6" title="In Theorem 2.2. ‣ Remark ‣ 2.2 Distance Bias ‣ 2 Theoretical Estimates for Rotary Positional Embedding (RoPE) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) is precisely <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{\lambda}-\Gamma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{\lambda}-\Gamma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>. For convenience, we denote it by:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\Delta_{\lambda,\Lambda}\eqqcolon\Gamma_{\lambda}-\Gamma_{\Lambda}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>≕</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\Delta_{\lambda,\Lambda}\eqqcolon\Gamma_{\lambda}-\Gamma_{\Lambda}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remark</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In addition to Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption A.1. ‣ Appendix A Preparations for proving Theorem , , and ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a>, if we further assume that <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{A_{i}\}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{A_{i}\}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{B_{j}\}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{B_{j}\}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> are sub-gaussian satisfying</p>
<table id="A1.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathbb{P}(|A_{i}-\mu_{0}|&gt;\eta)&lt;C_{1}e^{-C_{2}\eta^{2}},\quad\mathbb{P}(|B_{j}-\nu_{0}|&gt;\eta)&lt;C_{1}e^{-C_{2}\eta^{2}}\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathbb{P}(|A_{i}-\mu_{0}|&gt;\eta)&lt;C_{1}e^{-C_{2}\eta^{2}},\quad\mathbb{P}(|B_{j}-\nu_{0}|&gt;\eta)&lt;C_{1}e^{-C_{2}\eta^{2}}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for some <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1},C_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1},C_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{0},\nu_{0}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{0},\nu_{0}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math>, all <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i,j=0,\cdots,D/2-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i,j=0,\cdots,D/2-1</annotation></semantics></math>, then one can show<span id="footnote2" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">2</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">2</span>
              
              
              
            For example, using Laplace transform.</span></span></span> that the non-deterministic term <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\lambda}-Z_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\lambda}-Z_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> admits the following control</p>
<table id="A1.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.E20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathbb{P}(|Z_{\lambda}-Z_{\Lambda}|&gt;\eta)&lt;C_{3}e^{-C_{4}D\eta^{2}}\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mi>ℙ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathbb{P}(|Z_{\lambda}-Z_{\Lambda}|&gt;\eta)&lt;C_{3}e^{-C_{4}D\eta^{2}}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">for some <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{3},C_{4}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{3},C_{4}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and all <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. In other words, the magnitude of <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{\lambda}-Z_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{\lambda}-Z_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> is negligible (with high probability) compared to <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\lambda,\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\lambda,\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> is large.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1 (Long-Context Instability). ‣ 2.2 Distance Bias ‣ 2 Theoretical Estimates for Rotary Positional Embedding (RoPE) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1 (Long-Context Instability). ‣ 2.2 Distance Bias ‣ 2 Theoretical Estimates for Rotary Positional Embedding (RoPE) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">A direct computation of the expectation of <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Attn}_{\text{RoPE}}(q^{(m)},k^{(n)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mtext>RoPE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Attn}_{\text{RoPE}}(q^{(m)},k^{(n)})</annotation></semantics></math> gives:</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\frac{2}{\sqrt{D}}\mathbb{E}_{q^{(m)},k^{(n)}}\text{Attn}_{\text{RoPE}}(q^{(m)},k^{(n)})&amp;\eqqcolon\frac{2}{D}\sum_{d=0}^{D/2-1}\Big(\mu_{0}\cos 2\pi(m-n)\theta_{d}+\nu_{0}\sin 2\pi(m-n)\theta_{d}\Big)\\
&amp;=\frac{2\sqrt{\mu_{0}^{2}+\nu_{0}^{2}}}{D}\sum_{d=0}^{D/2-1}\sin\big(2\pi(m-n)\theta_{d}+\phi\big)\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mi>D</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mtext>RoPE</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≕</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\frac{2}{\sqrt{D}}\mathbb{E}_{q^{(m)},k^{(n)}}\text{Attn}_{\text{RoPE}}(q^{(m)},k^{(n)})&amp;\eqqcolon\frac{2}{D}\sum_{d=0}^{D/2-1}\Big(\mu_{0}\cos 2\pi(m-n)\theta_{d}+\nu_{0}\sin 2\pi(m-n)\theta_{d}\Big)\\
&amp;=\frac{2\sqrt{\mu_{0}^{2}+\nu_{0}^{2}}}{D}\sum_{d=0}^{D/2-1}\sin\big(2\pi(m-n)\theta_{d}+\phi\big)\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi=\arctan({\mu_{0}}/{\nu_{0}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arctan</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi=\arctan({\mu_{0}}/{\nu_{0}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=\arcsin(\gamma/\sqrt{\mu_{0}^{2}+\nu_{0}^{2}})/2\pi-\phi\mod 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>arcsin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo>mod</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=\arcsin(\gamma/\sqrt{\mu_{0}^{2}+\nu_{0}^{2}})/2\pi-\phi\mod 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\theta_{d}\}_{d=1}^{D/2-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\theta_{d}\}_{d=1}^{D/2-1}</annotation></semantics></math> are <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℚ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Q}</annotation></semantics></math>-linearly independent, it follows from Weyl’s criterion that <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\big((\lambda\theta_{1}),\cdots,(\lambda\theta_{D/2-1})\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\big((\lambda\theta_{1}),\cdots,(\lambda\theta_{D/2-1})\big)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=1,2,\cdots" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo lspace="0em">⋯</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=1,2,\cdots</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly distributed in <math id="A2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]^{D/2-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]^{D/2-1}</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g. Theorem 6.3 and Example 6.1 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kuipers &amp; Niederreiter (1974)</a></cite>). Here <math id="A2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r)</annotation></semantics></math> represents the fractional part of a real number <math id="A2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, for any <math id="A2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> we can find <math id="A2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\epsilon}\in\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\epsilon}\in\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently large such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E22"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\bigg|(\big(\lambda_{\epsilon}\theta_{1}),\cdots,(\lambda_{\epsilon}\theta_{D/2-1})\big)-(\beta,\cdots,\beta)\bigg|\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo mathsize="2.100em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo mathsize="2.100em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo mathsize="2.100em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo mathsize="2.100em">,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\bigg|(\big(\lambda_{\epsilon}\theta_{1}),\cdots,(\lambda_{\epsilon}\theta_{D/2-1})\big)-(\beta,\cdots,\beta)\bigg|\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">is so small that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\bigg|\frac{2}{D}\sum_{d=0}^{D/2-1}\sin\big(\lambda_{\epsilon}\theta^{2d/D}+\phi\big)-\frac{\gamma}{\sqrt{\mu_{0}^{2}+\nu_{0}^{2}}}\bigg|&lt;\epsilon+\mathcal{O}(\frac{1}{D}).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>γ</mi><msqrt><mrow><msubsup><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\bigg|\frac{2}{D}\sum_{d=0}^{D/2-1}\sin\big(\lambda_{\epsilon}\theta^{2d/D}+\phi\big)-\frac{\gamma}{\sqrt{\mu_{0}^{2}+\nu_{0}^{2}}}\bigg|&lt;\epsilon+\mathcal{O}(\frac{1}{D}).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Repeating this argument on a sequence <math id="A2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{k}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{k}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math> leads to the conclusion of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 2.1 (Long-Context Instability). ‣ 2.2 Distance Bias ‣ 2 Theoretical Estimates for Rotary Positional Embedding (RoPE) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2. ‣ Remark ‣ 2.2 Distance Bias ‣ 2 Theoretical Estimates for Rotary Positional Embedding (RoPE) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a></h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2. ‣ Remark ‣ 2.2 Distance Bias ‣ 2 Theoretical Estimates for Rotary Positional Embedding (RoPE) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> employs estimates of the following two sums:</p>
<table id="A3.EGx24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{C}_{D}(\lambda)\eqqcolon\frac{1}{D}\sum_{d=0}^{D/2-1}\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{2d/D},\\
\mathcal{S}_{D}(\lambda)\eqqcolon\frac{1}{D}\sum_{d=0}^{D/2-1}\sin 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{2d/D}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≕</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≕</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{C}_{D}(\lambda)\eqqcolon\frac{1}{D}\sum_{d=0}^{D/2-1}\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{2d/D},\\
\mathcal{S}_{D}(\lambda)\eqqcolon\frac{1}{D}\sum_{d=0}^{D/2-1}\sin 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{2d/D}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}&lt;1/10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}&lt;1/10</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D&gt;4|\log\theta_{0}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D&gt;4|\log\theta_{0}|</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, then the following inequalities hold:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}|\mathcal{C}_{D}(\lambda)|&amp;\leq\frac{2}{\theta_{0}|\log\theta_{0}|\lambda\pi}+\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha),\\
|\mathcal{S}_{D}(\lambda)|&amp;\leq\frac{2}{|\log\theta_{0}|}+\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}|\mathcal{C}_{D}(\lambda)|&amp;\leq\frac{2}{\theta_{0}|\log\theta_{0}|\lambda\pi}+\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha),\\
|\mathcal{S}_{D}(\lambda)|&amp;\leq\frac{2}{|\log\theta_{0}|}+\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for all <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, where</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)\eqqcolon\alpha+\frac{4\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\alpha}}{D}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≕</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)\eqqcolon\alpha+\frac{4\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\alpha}}{D}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma C.2</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}&lt;1/10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}&lt;1/10</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D&gt;4|\log\theta_{0}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D&gt;4|\log\theta_{0}|</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. If <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}&lt;1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}&lt;1/4</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{0}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{0}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, then we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx27" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E27"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{C}_{D}(\lambda)&gt;\frac{1}{2}\cdot(1-\epsilon_{0})\cdot\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}-\frac{1}{|\log\theta_{0}|}-\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{C}_{D}(\lambda)&gt;\frac{1}{2}\cdot(1-\epsilon_{0})\cdot\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}-\frac{1}{|\log\theta_{0}|}-\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">for all <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A3.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in (<a href="#A3.E26" title="In Lemma C.1. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The proofs of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a> and <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> will be given in Appendix <a href="#A5" title="Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E</span></a> and <a href="#A6" title="Appendix F Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2. ‣ Remark ‣ 2.2 Distance Bias ‣ 2 Theoretical Estimates for Rotary Positional Embedding (RoPE) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Choosing <math id="A3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{0}=1/4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{0}=1/4</annotation></semantics></math> and using <math id="A3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\theta_{0}^{1/4}&lt;1/8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\theta_{0}^{1/4}&lt;1/8</annotation></semantics></math>, it follows from Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx28" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{C}_{D}(\lambda)&amp;&gt;\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{3}{4}\cdot\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}-\frac{2}{|\log\theta_{0}|}-\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)\\
&amp;&gt;\frac{1}{4}-\frac{2}{|\log\theta_{0}|}-\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{C}_{D}(\lambda)&amp;&gt;\frac{1}{2}\cdot\frac{3}{4}\cdot\frac{\sqrt{2}}{2}-\frac{2}{|\log\theta_{0}|}-\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)\\
&amp;&gt;\frac{1}{4}-\frac{2}{|\log\theta_{0}|}-\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, using <math id="A3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda&gt;\theta_{0}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda&gt;\theta_{0}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> and Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx29" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{C}_{D}(\Lambda)&amp;&lt;\frac{2}{|\log\theta_{0}|}+\epsilon(D;\Lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{C}_{D}(\Lambda)&amp;&lt;\frac{2}{|\log\theta_{0}|}+\epsilon(D;\Lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">In addition, the following is a direct consequence of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx30" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{S}_{D}(\lambda)&lt;\frac{2}{|\log\theta_{0}|}+\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha),\\
\mathcal{S}_{D}(\Lambda)&lt;\frac{2}{|\log\theta_{0}|}+\epsilon(D;\Lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{S}_{D}(\lambda)&lt;\frac{2}{|\log\theta_{0}|}+\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha),\\
\mathcal{S}_{D}(\Lambda)&lt;\frac{2}{|\log\theta_{0}|}+\epsilon(D;\Lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining (<a href="#A3.E28" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>), (<a href="#A3.E29" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>), and (<a href="#A3.E30" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>), using the definition (<a href="#A1.E16" title="In Appendix A Preparations for proving Theorem , , and ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>), we bound <math id="A3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{sgn}(\mu_{0})\Delta_{\lambda,\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>sgn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{sgn}(\mu_{0})\Delta_{\lambda,\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="A3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{\lambda,\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{\lambda,\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in (<a href="#A1.E18" title="In Appendix A Preparations for proving Theorem , , and ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>)) from below as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\text{sgn}(\mu_{0})\Delta_{\lambda,\Lambda}&amp;\geq\mathcal{C}_{D}(\lambda)\cdot|\mu_{0}|-|\mathcal{C}_{D}(\Lambda)\cdot\mu_{0}|-|\mathcal{S}_{D}(\lambda)\cdot\nu_{0}|-|\mathcal{S}_{D}(\Lambda)\cdot\nu_{0}|\\
&amp;&gt;\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{4}-\frac{4(|\mu_{0}|+|\nu_{0}|)}{|\log\theta_{0}|}-2(|\mu_{0}|+|\nu_{0}|)\cdot\Big(\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)+\epsilon(D;\Lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)\Big).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mtext>sgn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\text{sgn}(\mu_{0})\Delta_{\lambda,\Lambda}&amp;\geq\mathcal{C}_{D}(\lambda)\cdot|\mu_{0}|-|\mathcal{C}_{D}(\Lambda)\cdot\mu_{0}|-|\mathcal{S}_{D}(\lambda)\cdot\nu_{0}|-|\mathcal{S}_{D}(\Lambda)\cdot\nu_{0}|\\
&amp;&gt;\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{4}-\frac{4(|\mu_{0}|+|\nu_{0}|)}{|\log\theta_{0}|}-2(|\mu_{0}|+|\nu_{0}|)\cdot\Big(\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)+\epsilon(D;\Lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)\Big).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">By first choosing <math id="A3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A3.p4.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\theta_{0}&lt;\exp(-{64(|\mu_{0}|+|\nu_{0}|)}/{|\mu_{0}|})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>64</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">/</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}&lt;\exp(-{64(|\mu_{0}|+|\nu_{0}|)}/{|\mu_{0}|})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx32" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\frac{4(|\mu_{0}|+|\nu_{0}|)}{|\log\theta_{0}|}&lt;\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{16},\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\frac{4(|\mu_{0}|+|\nu_{0}|)}{|\log\theta_{0}|}&lt;\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{16},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">and then increasing <math id="A3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx33" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}2(|\mu_{0}|+|\nu_{0}|)\cdot\Big(\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)+\epsilon(D;\Lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)\Big)&lt;\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{16}\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}2(|\mu_{0}|+|\nu_{0}|)\cdot\Big(\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)+\epsilon(D;\Lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)\Big)&lt;\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{16}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">for some properly chosen <math id="A3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> (e.g. <math id="A3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=0</annotation></semantics></math>), we arrive at</span></p>
<table id="A3.EGx34" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.E34"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.E34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\text{sgn}(\mu_{0})\Delta_{\lambda,\Lambda}&gt;\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{4}-\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{16}-\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{16}=\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{8}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>sgn</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>16</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\text{sgn}(\mu_{0})\Delta_{\lambda,\Lambda}&gt;\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{4}-\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{16}-\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{16}=\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{8}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(34)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">Thus Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 2.2. ‣ Remark ‣ 2.2 Distance Bias ‣ 2 Theoretical Estimates for Rotary Positional Embedding (RoPE) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a> is concluded.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ Remark ‣ 2.2 Distance Bias ‣ 2 Theoretical Estimates for Rotary Positional Embedding (RoPE) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a></h2>

<div id="A4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition of <math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{D}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{D}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> from (<a href="#A3.E24" title="In Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>), we have the trivial bound</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx35" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{C}_{D}(\lambda)&lt;\frac{1}{2}\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{C}_{D}(\lambda)&lt;\frac{1}{2}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(35)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">holds for all <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>. Now choose <math id="A4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to be sufficiently small such that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx36" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\max(\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}},\Lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}})&lt;\frac{1}{4},\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\max(\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}},\Lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}})&lt;\frac{1}{4},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(36)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">for some <math id="A4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to be determined later. Then using (<a href="#A4.E35" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">35</span></a>) and (<a href="#A4.E36" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>), we can apply Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> to see that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx37" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E37"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\Delta_{\lambda,\Lambda}&amp;&lt;\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{2}-\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{2}\cdot(1-\epsilon_{0})\cdot\cos 2\pi\Lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}-\epsilon(D;\Lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)|\mu_{0}|,\\
-\Delta_{\lambda,\Lambda}&amp;&lt;\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{2}-\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{2}\cdot(1-\epsilon_{0})\cdot\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}-\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)|\mu_{0}|.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\Delta_{\lambda,\Lambda}&amp;&lt;\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{2}-\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{2}\cdot(1-\epsilon_{0})\cdot\cos 2\pi\Lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}-\epsilon(D;\Lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)|\mu_{0}|,\\
-\Delta_{\lambda,\Lambda}&amp;&lt;\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{2}-\frac{|\mu_{0}|}{2}\cdot(1-\epsilon_{0})\cdot\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}-\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)|\mu_{0}|.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(37)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">By first choosing <math id="A4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon_{0}&lt;\frac{\epsilon}{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon_{0}&lt;\frac{\epsilon}{4}</annotation></semantics></math>, then further decreasing <math id="A4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx38" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;|\mu_{0}|\cos 2\pi\Lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}&gt;|\mu_{0}|-\frac{\epsilon}{4},\\
&amp;|\mu_{0}|\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}&gt;|\mu_{0}|-\frac{\epsilon}{4},\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;|\mu_{0}|\cos 2\pi\Lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}&gt;|\mu_{0}|-\frac{\epsilon}{4},\\
&amp;|\mu_{0}|\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}&gt;|\mu_{0}|-\frac{\epsilon}{4},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(38)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">and lastly increasing <math id="A4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx39" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)|\mu_{0}|&lt;\epsilon/4,\\
\epsilon(D;\Lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)|\mu_{0}|&lt;\epsilon/4,\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)|\mu_{0}|&lt;\epsilon/4,\\
\epsilon(D;\Lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)|\mu_{0}|&lt;\epsilon/4,\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(39)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx40" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}|\Delta_{\lambda,\Lambda}|&lt;\epsilon,\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}|\Delta_{\lambda,\Lambda}|&lt;\epsilon,\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(40)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">which proves Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ Remark ‣ 2.2 Distance Bias ‣ 2 Theoretical Estimates for Rotary Positional Embedding (RoPE) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Remark</h4>

<div id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">One can directly verify Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 2.3. ‣ Remark ‣ 2.2 Distance Bias ‣ 2 Theoretical Estimates for Rotary Positional Embedding (RoPE) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a> using the following elementary facts</p>
<table id="A4.EGx41" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\lim_{\theta_{0}\to 0}\mathcal{C}_{D}&amp;={(\cos 2\pi\lambda+D/2-1)}/{D},\\
\lim_{\theta_{0}\to 0}\mathcal{S}_{D}&amp;={\sin 2\pi\lambda}/{D}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\lim_{\theta_{0}\to 0}\mathcal{C}_{D}&amp;={(\cos 2\pi\lambda+D/2-1)}/{D},\\
\lim_{\theta_{0}\to 0}\mathcal{S}_{D}&amp;={\sin 2\pi\lambda}/{D}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(41)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Namely, choose a sufficiently large <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4/D&lt;\epsilon/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4/D&lt;\epsilon/2</annotation></semantics></math>, and then choose <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently small. But such argument lacks a quantitative understanding of the limiting behavior and the relation among the variables in question. We adopt an alternative proof above using Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a> to explicitly quantify the smallness of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> in terms of <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Without ambiguity and for simplicity, drop <math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> from the expressions of <math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{D}(\lambda),\mathcal{S}_{D}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{D}(\lambda),\mathcal{S}_{D}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> throughout the proof. First let us focus on <math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{D}</annotation></semantics></math>. By treating <math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> as a Riemann sum we can rewrite it as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx42" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{C}_{D}&amp;=\bigg(\frac{1}{D}\sum_{d=0}^{D/2}\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{2d/D}-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{x}dx\bigg)+\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{x}dx\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{d=0}^{D/2}\int_{2d/D}^{2(d+1)/D}\Big(\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{2d/D}-\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{x}\Big)dx+\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{x}dx\\
&amp;\eqqcolon\frac{1}{2}\Delta+\frac{1}{2}\mathcal{I}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mn>0</mn><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≕</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathcal{C}_{D}&amp;=\bigg(\frac{1}{D}\sum_{d=0}^{D/2}\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{2d/D}-\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{x}dx\bigg)+\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{x}dx\\
&amp;=\frac{1}{2}\sum_{d=0}^{D/2}\int_{2d/D}^{2(d+1)/D}\Big(\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{2d/D}-\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{x}\Big)dx+\frac{1}{2}\int_{0}^{1}\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{x}dx\\
&amp;\eqqcolon\frac{1}{2}\Delta+\frac{1}{2}\mathcal{I}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(42)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">We first consider <math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\eqqcolon\sum_{d=0}^{D/2}\Delta_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">≕</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\eqqcolon\sum_{d=0}^{D/2}\Delta_{d}</annotation></semantics></math>. For arbitrary <math id="A5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> we may split the sum into two parts:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E43"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\Delta=\sum_{d\leq\alpha D/2}\Delta_{d}+\sum_{d&gt;\alpha D/2}\Delta_{d}\eqqcolon\Delta^{\prime}+\Delta^{\prime\prime}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>≕</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\Delta=\sum_{d\leq\alpha D/2}\Delta_{d}+\sum_{d&gt;\alpha D/2}\Delta_{d}\eqqcolon\Delta^{\prime}+\Delta^{\prime\prime}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(43)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">For each term in <math id="A5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we use the fact that cosine functions are bounded by <math id="A5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> and control it as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E44"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}|\Delta_{d}|\leq\frac{2}{D}\cdot 2=\frac{4}{D}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}|\Delta_{d}|\leq\frac{2}{D}\cdot 2=\frac{4}{D}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(44)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">For each term in <math id="A5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, we instead use the Lipschitz bound of the integrand:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E45"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}|\Delta_{d}|\leq\text{Lip}_{d}\cdot\frac{4}{D^{2}},\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>Lip</mtext><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}|\Delta_{d}|\leq\text{Lip}_{d}\cdot\frac{4}{D^{2}},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(45)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E46"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\text{Lip}_{d}\eqqcolon\sup_{[\frac{2d}{D},\frac{2(d+1)}{D}]}|\frac{d}{dx}\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{x}|=2\pi\lambda|\log\theta_{0}\cdot\theta_{0}^{x}\sin 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{x}|\leq 2\pi\lambda|\log\theta_{0}|\theta_{0}^{2d/D}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>Lip</mtext><mi>d</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">≕</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\text{Lip}_{d}\eqqcolon\sup_{[\frac{2d}{D},\frac{2(d+1)}{D}]}|\frac{d}{dx}\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{x}|=2\pi\lambda|\log\theta_{0}\cdot\theta_{0}^{x}\sin 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{x}|\leq 2\pi\lambda|\log\theta_{0}|\theta_{0}^{2d/D}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(46)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">Now plugging both (<a href="#A5.E44" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">44</span></a>) and (<a href="#A5.E45" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">45</span></a>) into (<a href="#A5.E43" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>), we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E47"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}|\Delta^{\prime}|&amp;\leq\frac{D\alpha}{2}\cdot\frac{4}{D}=2\alpha,\\
|\Delta^{\prime\prime}|&amp;\leq\frac{4}{D^{2}}\cdot 2\pi\lambda|\log\theta_{0}|\cdot\sum_{d=D\alpha/2+1}^{D/2}\theta_{0}^{2d/D}\\
&amp;\leq\frac{4}{D^{2}}\cdot 2\pi\lambda|\log\theta_{0}|\cdot\theta_{0}^{\frac{2}{D}(\frac{D\alpha}{2}+1)}\cdot\frac{1}{1-\theta_{0}^{2/D}}\\
&amp;\leq\frac{8\pi\lambda|\log\theta_{0}|}{D^{2}}\cdot\theta_{0}^{\alpha}\cdot(\frac{1}{1-\theta_{0}^{2/D}}-1).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munderover></mstyle><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}|\Delta^{\prime}|&amp;\leq\frac{D\alpha}{2}\cdot\frac{4}{D}=2\alpha,\\
|\Delta^{\prime\prime}|&amp;\leq\frac{4}{D^{2}}\cdot 2\pi\lambda|\log\theta_{0}|\cdot\sum_{d=D\alpha/2+1}^{D/2}\theta_{0}^{2d/D}\\
&amp;\leq\frac{4}{D^{2}}\cdot 2\pi\lambda|\log\theta_{0}|\cdot\theta_{0}^{\frac{2}{D}(\frac{D\alpha}{2}+1)}\cdot\frac{1}{1-\theta_{0}^{2/D}}\\
&amp;\leq\frac{8\pi\lambda|\log\theta_{0}|}{D^{2}}\cdot\theta_{0}^{\alpha}\cdot(\frac{1}{1-\theta_{0}^{2/D}}-1).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(47)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">Using 2nd order Taylor’s expansion with remainder of Lagrange form, we obtain that</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}1-\theta_{0}^{2/D}\geq|\log\theta_{0}|\cdot\frac{2}{D}-|\log\theta_{0}|^{2}\cdot\frac{4}{D^{2}}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>D</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}1-\theta_{0}^{2/D}\geq|\log\theta_{0}|\cdot\frac{2}{D}-|\log\theta_{0}|^{2}\cdot\frac{4}{D^{2}}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(48)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.8.1" class="ltx_text">Here we have used the following fact:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E49"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\sup_{x\in[0,\frac{2}{D}]}|\frac{d^{2}}{dx^{2}}\theta_{0}^{x}|\leq|\log\theta_{0}|^{2}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\sup_{x\in[0,\frac{2}{D}]}|\frac{d^{2}}{dx^{2}}\theta_{0}^{x}|\leq|\log\theta_{0}|^{2}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(49)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.9.1" class="ltx_text">Now inserting (<a href="#A5.E49" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">49</span></a>) into the estimate of <math id="A5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta^{\prime\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta^{\prime\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A5.E47" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">47</span></a>), we get</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}|\Delta^{\prime\prime}|\leq\frac{4\pi\lambda}{D}\cdot\theta_{0}^{\alpha}\cdot\frac{1}{1-2|\log\theta_{0}|/D}\leq\frac{4\pi\lambda}{D}\cdot\theta_{0}^{\alpha}\cdot\frac{1}{1-1/2}=\frac{8\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\alpha}}{D}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}|\Delta^{\prime\prime}|\leq\frac{4\pi\lambda}{D}\cdot\theta_{0}^{\alpha}\cdot\frac{1}{1-2|\log\theta_{0}|/D}\leq\frac{4\pi\lambda}{D}\cdot\theta_{0}^{\alpha}\cdot\frac{1}{1-1/2}=\frac{8\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\alpha}}{D}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(50)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.10.1" class="ltx_text">We have now arrived at the bound for the first term in (<a href="#A5.E43" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">43</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E51"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}|\frac{\Delta}{2}|\leq\alpha+\frac{4\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\alpha}}{D}\eqqcolon\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≕</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}|\frac{\Delta}{2}|\leq\alpha+\frac{4\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\alpha}}{D}\eqqcolon\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(51)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.11.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha)</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in (<a href="#A3.E26" title="In Lemma C.1. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>) and <math id="A5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> is arbitrary. Next, we estimate the integral term in (<a href="#A5.E42" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>).
By performing a change of variable <math id="A5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\theta_{0}^{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\theta_{0}^{x}</annotation></semantics></math> we see that</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E52"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E52.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\frac{1}{2}\cdot\mathcal{I}=\frac{1}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\int_{\theta_{0}}^{1}\frac{\cos 2\pi\lambda y}{y}dy=\frac{1}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\int_{\lambda\theta_{0}}^{\lambda}\frac{\cos 2\pi y}{y}dy.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mn>1</mn></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>λ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\frac{1}{2}\cdot\mathcal{I}=\frac{1}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\int_{\theta_{0}}^{1}\frac{\cos 2\pi\lambda y}{y}dy=\frac{1}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\int_{\lambda\theta_{0}}^{\lambda}\frac{\cos 2\pi y}{y}dy.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(52)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.12.1" class="ltx_text">Note the right hand side of (<a href="#A5.E52" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>) is an oscillatory integral, so we may employ the cancellation effect to control it. Define</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E53"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E53.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}n_{0}&amp;=\min\{n\in\mathbb{Z}:\lambda\theta_{0}\leq\frac{1}{4}(4n+1)\},\\
N_{0}&amp;=\max\{n\in\mathbb{Z}:\lambda\geq\frac{1}{4}(4n+5)\}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}n_{0}&amp;=\min\{n\in\mathbb{Z}:\lambda\theta_{0}\leq\frac{1}{4}(4n+1)\},\\
N_{0}&amp;=\max\{n\in\mathbb{Z}:\lambda\geq\frac{1}{4}(4n+5)\}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(53)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.13" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.13.1" class="ltx_text">Decompose the integration interval of (<a href="#A5.E52" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>) as follows (for brevity we omit the integrand):</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E54"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\int_{\lambda\theta_{0}}^{\frac{1}{4}(4n_{0}+1)}+\sum_{n=n_{0}}^{N_{0}}\big(\int_{\frac{1}{4}(4n+1)}^{\frac{1}{4}(4n+3)}+\int_{\frac{1}{4}(4n+3)}^{\frac{1}{4}(4n+5)}\big)+\int_{\frac{1}{4}(4N_{0}+5)}^{\lambda}\\
=&amp;I_{*}+\sum_{n=n_{0}}^{N_{0}}(I_{n}^{-}+I_{n}^{+})+I^{*}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mphantom></mphantom></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\int_{\lambda\theta_{0}}^{\frac{1}{4}(4n_{0}+1)}+\sum_{n=n_{0}}^{N_{0}}\big(\int_{\frac{1}{4}(4n+1)}^{\frac{1}{4}(4n+3)}+\int_{\frac{1}{4}(4n+3)}^{\frac{1}{4}(4n+5)}\big)+\int_{\frac{1}{4}(4N_{0}+5)}^{\lambda}\\
=&amp;I_{*}+\sum_{n=n_{0}}^{N_{0}}(I_{n}^{-}+I_{n}^{+})+I^{*}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(54)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.14" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.14.1" class="ltx_text">According to (<a href="#A5.E53" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a>), integrals <math id="A5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> contain at most a full period of <math id="A5.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos 2\pi y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos 2\pi y</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore can be trivially bounded:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E55"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}|I^{*}|+|I_{*}|\leq\frac{1}{\lambda\theta_{0}}+\frac{1}{\lambda-1}\leq\frac{2}{\lambda\theta_{0}}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}|I^{*}|+|I_{*}|\leq\frac{1}{\lambda\theta_{0}}+\frac{1}{\lambda-1}\leq\frac{2}{\lambda\theta_{0}}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(55)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.15" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.15.1" class="ltx_text">Here we used the assumption that <math id="A5.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{0}&lt;1/10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{0}&lt;1/10</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> in the second inequality above.
For the sum term in the middle, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E56"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}|I_{n}^{-}+I_{n}^{+}|=|I_{n}^{-}|-|I_{n}^{+}|\leq\frac{4}{4n+1}\cdot\frac{1}{\pi}-\frac{4}{4n+5}\cdot\frac{1}{\pi}\leq\frac{1}{\pi}\cdot\frac{1}{n^{2}}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}|I_{n}^{-}+I_{n}^{+}|=|I_{n}^{-}|-|I_{n}^{+}|\leq\frac{4}{4n+1}\cdot\frac{1}{\pi}-\frac{4}{4n+5}\cdot\frac{1}{\pi}\leq\frac{1}{\pi}\cdot\frac{1}{n^{2}}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(56)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.16" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.16.1" class="ltx_text">Here we used the fact that <math id="A5.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos 2\pi y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos 2\pi y</annotation></semantics></math> is constantly non-positive on the integral range of <math id="A5.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{n}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{n}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E57"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}|I_{n}^{-}|=-\int_{\frac{4n+1}{4}}^{\frac{4n+3}{4}}\frac{\cos 2\pi y}{y}dy\leq-\frac{4}{4n+1}\int_{\frac{4n+1}{4}}^{\frac{4n+3}{4}}\cos 2\pi ydy=\frac{4}{4n+1}\cdot\frac{1}{\pi}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}|I_{n}^{-}|=-\int_{\frac{4n+1}{4}}^{\frac{4n+3}{4}}\frac{\cos 2\pi y}{y}dy\leq-\frac{4}{4n+1}\int_{\frac{4n+1}{4}}^{\frac{4n+3}{4}}\cos 2\pi ydy=\frac{4}{4n+1}\cdot\frac{1}{\pi}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(57)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p1.17" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.17.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, <math id="A5.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos 2\pi y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos 2\pi y</annotation></semantics></math> is constantly non-negative on the integral range of <math id="A5.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{n}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{n}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, and thus</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E58"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}-|I_{n}^{+}|=-\int_{\frac{4n+3}{4}}^{\frac{4n+5}{4}}\frac{\cos 2\pi y}{y}dy\leq-\frac{4}{4n+5}\int_{\frac{4n+3}{4}}^{\frac{4n+5}{4}}\cos 2\pi ydy=\frac{4}{4n+5}\cdot\frac{1}{\pi}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>I</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msup><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0em">≤</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mi>y</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}-|I_{n}^{+}|=-\int_{\frac{4n+3}{4}}^{\frac{4n+5}{4}}\frac{\cos 2\pi y}{y}dy\leq-\frac{4}{4n+5}\int_{\frac{4n+3}{4}}^{\frac{4n+5}{4}}\cos 2\pi ydy=\frac{4}{4n+5}\cdot\frac{1}{\pi}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(58)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">so the sum admits the following bound:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E59"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\sum_{n=n_{0}}^{N_{0}}(I_{n}^{-}+I_{n}^{+})\leq\frac{1}{\pi}\sum_{n=n_{0}}^{N_{0}}\frac{1}{n^{2}}\leq\frac{1}{\pi}\cdot\frac{1}{n_{0}-1}\leq\frac{1}{\pi}\cdot\frac{2}{\lambda\theta_{0}},\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>n</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\sum_{n=n_{0}}^{N_{0}}(I_{n}^{-}+I_{n}^{+})\leq\frac{1}{\pi}\sum_{n=n_{0}}^{N_{0}}\frac{1}{n^{2}}\leq\frac{1}{\pi}\cdot\frac{1}{n_{0}-1}\leq\frac{1}{\pi}\cdot\frac{2}{\lambda\theta_{0}},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(59)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where we used the first identity in (<a href="#A5.E53" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">53</span></a>). Inserting (<a href="#A5.E55" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">55</span></a>) and (<a href="#A5.E59" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">59</span></a>) into (<a href="#A5.E52" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E60"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\frac{1}{2}\cdot\mathcal{I}\leq\frac{2}{\theta_{0}|\log\theta_{0}|\lambda\pi}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\frac{1}{2}\cdot\mathcal{I}\leq\frac{2}{\theta_{0}|\log\theta_{0}|\lambda\pi}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(60)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">Combining (<a href="#A5.E51" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>) and (<a href="#A5.E60" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">60</span></a>), we concluded the estimate of <math id="A5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A3.E25" title="In Lemma C.1. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>). Next we estimate <math id="A5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{D}</annotation></semantics></math>. We point out that most the proofs of bounding <math id="A5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> follows the same line as that of <math id="A5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, so to avoid repetitive argument, therefore we state without proving all results that are achievable through same techniques as its <math id="A5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> counterpart, and only focus on addressing the difference.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, we conduct a similar decomposition of <math id="A5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> as (<a href="#A5.E42" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>), into <math id="A5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\Delta}{2}+\frac{\mathcal{I}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\Delta}{2}+\frac{\mathcal{I}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. The estimate of <math id="A5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta</annotation></semantics></math> follows from exactly the same lines as that of <math id="A5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}_{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence we omit the details:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E61"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\frac{\Delta}{2}\leq\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\frac{\Delta}{2}\leq\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(61)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">To estimate <math id="A5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathcal{I}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathcal{I}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we again use the change of variable <math id="A5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y=\theta_{0}^{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><mi>x</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y=\theta_{0}^{x}</annotation></semantics></math> and similar to (<a href="#A5.E52" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>) we get</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E62"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\frac{\mathcal{I}}{2}=\frac{1}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\int_{\lambda\theta_{0}}^{\lambda}\frac{\sin 2\pi y}{y}dy.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mi>λ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\frac{\mathcal{I}}{2}=\frac{1}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\int_{\lambda\theta_{0}}^{\lambda}\frac{\sin 2\pi y}{y}dy.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(62)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">To bound this oscillatory integral we adopt the following decomposition of integral region:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E63"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\int_{\lambda\theta_{0}}^{1/2}+\sum_{n=0}^{N_{0}}\big(\int_{\frac{1}{2}(2n+1)}^{\frac{1}{2}(2n+2)}+\int_{\frac{1}{2}(2n+2)}^{\frac{1}{2}(2n+3)}\big)+\int_{\frac{1}{2}(2N_{0}+3)}^{\lambda}\\
=&amp;I_{*}+\sum_{n=0}^{N_{0}}(I_{n}^{-}+I_{n}^{+})+I^{*},\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mphantom></mphantom></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\int_{\lambda\theta_{0}}^{1/2}+\sum_{n=0}^{N_{0}}\big(\int_{\frac{1}{2}(2n+1)}^{\frac{1}{2}(2n+2)}+\int_{\frac{1}{2}(2n+2)}^{\frac{1}{2}(2n+3)}\big)+\int_{\frac{1}{2}(2N_{0}+3)}^{\lambda}\\
=&amp;I_{*}+\sum_{n=0}^{N_{0}}(I_{n}^{-}+I_{n}^{+})+I^{*},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(63)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E64"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}N_{0}=\max\{n\in\mathbb{Z}:\lambda\geq\frac{1}{2}(2n+3)\}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}N_{0}=\max\{n\in\mathbb{Z}:\lambda\geq\frac{1}{2}(2n+3)\}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(64)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.5.1" class="ltx_text">Note again that the integrand is non-positive in <math id="A5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{n}^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{n}^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>, and non-negative in <math id="A5.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{n}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{n}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. Similar to (<a href="#A5.E55" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">55</span></a>) we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E65"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}|I_{n}^{-}+I_{n}^{+}|\leq\frac{1}{\pi}\cdot|-\frac{2}{2n+1}+\frac{2}{2n+3}|=\frac{1}{\pi}\cdot\frac{4}{(2n+1)(2n+3)}&lt;\frac{1}{\pi}\cdot\frac{1}{n^{2}},\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}|I_{n}^{-}+I_{n}^{+}|\leq\frac{1}{\pi}\cdot|-\frac{2}{2n+1}+\frac{2}{2n+3}|=\frac{1}{\pi}\cdot\frac{4}{(2n+1)(2n+3)}&lt;\frac{1}{\pi}\cdot\frac{1}{n^{2}},\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(65)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">and therefore</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E66"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\sum_{n=0}^{N_{0}}(I_{n}^{-}+I_{n}^{+})&lt;\frac{1}{\pi}\sum_{n=0}^{N_{0}}\frac{1}{n^{2}}&lt;\frac{\pi}{6}&lt;1.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>I</mi><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>π</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\sum_{n=0}^{N_{0}}(I_{n}^{-}+I_{n}^{+})&lt;\frac{1}{\pi}\sum_{n=0}^{N_{0}}\frac{1}{n^{2}}&lt;\frac{\pi}{6}&lt;1.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(66)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.7.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we use the fact that <math id="A5.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\sin 2\pi y}/{y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>sin</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\sin 2\pi y}/{y}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded by <math id="A5.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> on the interval <math id="A5.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1/2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1/2]</annotation></semantics></math> to trivially bound <math id="A5.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{*}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E67"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}|I_{*}|\leq\frac{1}{2}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}|I_{*}|\leq\frac{1}{2}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(67)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.8.1" class="ltx_text">The integral in the last term contains at most a full period, and thus admits the following bound:</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E68"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}|I^{*}|&lt;\frac{1}{\lambda-1}\leq 1.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mi>I</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}|I^{*}|&lt;\frac{1}{\lambda-1}\leq 1.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(68)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.9.1" class="ltx_text">Combining (<a href="#A5.E66" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">66</span></a>), (<a href="#A5.E67" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">67</span></a>), and (<a href="#A5.E68" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">68</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.E69"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\frac{\mathcal{I}}{2}&lt;\frac{2}{|\log\theta_{0}|}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\frac{\mathcal{I}}{2}&lt;\frac{2}{|\log\theta_{0}|}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(69)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.p3.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p3.10.1" class="ltx_text">Lastly, combining (<a href="#A5.E61" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">61</span></a>) and (<a href="#A5.E69" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">69</span></a>), we proved the estimates of <math id="A5.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}_{D}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#A3.E25" title="In Lemma C.1. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a>). Thus we concluded Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem1" title="Lemma C.1. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.1</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a></h2>

<div id="A6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof reuses the decomposition (<a href="#A5.E42" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">42</span></a>) and the bound (<a href="#A5.E51" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>), but further needs a lower bound for <math id="A6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\mathcal{I}}/{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\mathcal{I}}/{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
First we decompose the right hand side integral of (<a href="#A5.E52" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">52</span></a>) as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E70"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\frac{1}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\bigg(\int_{\lambda\theta_{0}}^{1/4}+\int_{1/4}^{\lambda}\bigg)\frac{\cos 2\pi y}{y}dy.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>λ</mi></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\frac{1}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\bigg(\int_{\lambda\theta_{0}}^{1/4}+\int_{1/4}^{\lambda}\bigg)\frac{\cos 2\pi y}{y}dy.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(70)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Following the same argument to bound the middle term in (<a href="#A5.E66" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">66</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E71"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E71.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}|\frac{1}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\int_{1/4}^{\lambda}\frac{\cos 2\pi y}{y}dy|&lt;\frac{1}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\cdot 2=\frac{1}{|\log\theta_{0}|}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mi>λ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}|\frac{1}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\int_{1/4}^{\lambda}\frac{\cos 2\pi y}{y}dy|&lt;\frac{1}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\cdot 2=\frac{1}{|\log\theta_{0}|}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(71)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, notice that the integrand stays positive on <math id="A6.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[\lambda\theta_{0},1/4]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[\lambda\theta_{0},1/4]</annotation></semantics></math>, we hence have</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\frac{1}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\int_{\lambda\theta_{0}}^{1/4}\frac{\cos 2\pi y}{y}dy&gt;\frac{1}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\int_{\lambda\theta_{0}}^{\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}}\frac{\cos 2\pi y}{y}dy&gt;\frac{\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\cdot\int_{\lambda\theta_{0}}^{\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}}\frac{dy}{y}\\
=&amp;\frac{\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\cdot|\log\theta_{0}|(1-\epsilon_{0})=\frac{1}{2}\cdot(1-\epsilon_{0})\cdot\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mphantom></mphantom></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}&amp;\frac{1}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\int_{\lambda\theta_{0}}^{1/4}\frac{\cos 2\pi y}{y}dy&gt;\frac{1}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\int_{\lambda\theta_{0}}^{\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}}\frac{\cos 2\pi y}{y}dy&gt;\frac{\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\cdot\int_{\lambda\theta_{0}}^{\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}}\frac{dy}{y}\\
=&amp;\frac{\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\cdot|\log\theta_{0}|(1-\epsilon_{0})=\frac{1}{2}\cdot(1-\epsilon_{0})\cdot\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(72)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, combining (<a href="#A5.E51" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix E Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">51</span></a>), (<a href="#A6.E71" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix F Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">71</span></a>), and (<a href="#A6.E72" title="In Proof of Lemma . ‣ Appendix F Proof of Lemma ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">72</span></a>), we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A6.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.E73"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.E73.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}|\mathcal{C}_{D}|&amp;\geq\frac{1}{2}\mathcal{I}-\frac{1}{2}|\Delta|\geq\frac{1}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\int_{\lambda\theta_{0}}^{1/4}\frac{\cos 2\pi y}{y}dy-|\frac{1}{2\log\theta_{0}}\int_{1/4}^{\lambda}\frac{\cos 2\pi y}{y}dy|-\frac{1}{2}|\Delta|\\
&amp;\geq(1-\epsilon_{0})\cdot\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}-\frac{1}{|\log\theta_{0}|}-\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℐ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msubsup><mo>∫</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><mi>λ</mi></msubsup></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>y</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo rspace="0em">d</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn><msub><mi>ϵ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}|\mathcal{C}_{D}|&amp;\geq\frac{1}{2}\mathcal{I}-\frac{1}{2}|\Delta|\geq\frac{1}{2|\log\theta_{0}|}\int_{\lambda\theta_{0}}^{1/4}\frac{\cos 2\pi y}{y}dy-|\frac{1}{2\log\theta_{0}}\int_{1/4}^{\lambda}\frac{\cos 2\pi y}{y}dy|-\frac{1}{2}|\Delta|\\
&amp;\geq(1-\epsilon_{0})\cdot\cos 2\pi\lambda\theta_{0}^{\epsilon_{0}}-\frac{1}{|\log\theta_{0}|}-\epsilon(D;\lambda,\theta_{0},\alpha),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(73)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">which is exactly (<a href="#A3.E27" title="In Lemma C.2. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>), and hence proved Lemma <a href="#A3.Thmtheorem2" title="Lemma C.2. ‣ Appendix C Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">C.2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2 (Decaying Bias). ‣ 3 A New Positional Encoding Method: Token-Aware Phase Attention (TAPA) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a></h2>

<div id="A7.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2 (Decaying Bias). ‣ 3 A New Positional Encoding Method: Token-Aware Phase Attention (TAPA) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">For convenience, we introduce the following notations:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E74"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E74.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}x_{A}\coloneqq(q_{A},k_{A}),\quad x_{P}\coloneqq(q_{P},k_{P}).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}x_{A}\coloneqq(q_{A},k_{A}),\quad x_{P}\coloneqq(q_{P},k_{P}).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(74)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">First let us expand the expression of the expectation of TAPA:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E75"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\int_{x_{A}}\frac{x_{A}^{\top}\cdot J_{\theta D}\cdot x_{A}}{\sqrt{\theta D}}\bigg(\int_{x_{P}}\cos\Big(\frac{2\pi|m-n|^{\alpha}}{\sqrt{(1-\theta)D}}\cdot x_{P}^{\top}\cdot J_{(1-\theta)D}\cdot x_{P}\Big)\cdot\rho(x_{A},x_{P})dx_{P}\bigg)dx_{A}\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo mathsize="0.700em">,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\int_{x_{A}}\frac{x_{A}^{\top}\cdot J_{\theta D}\cdot x_{A}}{\sqrt{\theta D}}\bigg(\int_{x_{P}}\cos\Big(\frac{2\pi|m-n|^{\alpha}}{\sqrt{(1-\theta)D}}\cdot x_{P}^{\top}\cdot J_{(1-\theta)D}\cdot x_{P}\Big)\cdot\rho(x_{A},x_{P})dx_{P}\bigg)dx_{A}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(75)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{d}=\begin{pmatrix}\mathbf{0}&amp;I_{d}\\
I_{d}&amp;\mathbf{0}\end{pmatrix}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>d</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{d}=\begin{pmatrix}\mathbf{0}&amp;I_{d}\\
I_{d}&amp;\mathbf{0}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let us further simplify the expression by writing <math id="A7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\eqqcolon\frac{2|m-n|^{\alpha}}{\sqrt{(1-\theta)D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≕</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\eqqcolon\frac{2|m-n|^{\alpha}}{\sqrt{(1-\theta)D}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The inner integral of (<a href="#A7.E75" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix G Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">75</span></a>) can now written as</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E76"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E76.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\int_{x_{P}}\cos\Big(\pi\lambda\cdot x_{P}^{\top}\cdot J\cdot x_{P}\Big)\cdot\rho(x_{A},x_{P})dx_{P}=\text{Re}\bigg(\int_{x_{P}}e^{-i\pi\lambda\cdot x_{P}^{\top}\cdot J\cdot x_{P}}\cdot\rho(x_{A},x_{P})dx_{P}\bigg).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></msub><mi>cos</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext>Re</mtext><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\int_{x_{P}}\cos\Big(\pi\lambda\cdot x_{P}^{\top}\cdot J\cdot x_{P}\Big)\cdot\rho(x_{A},x_{P})dx_{P}=\text{Re}\bigg(\int_{x_{P}}e^{-i\pi\lambda\cdot x_{P}^{\top}\cdot J\cdot x_{P}}\cdot\rho(x_{A},x_{P})dx_{P}\bigg).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(76)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">where we omitted the subscript <math id="A7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\theta)D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\theta)D</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>J</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J</annotation></semantics></math> when there is no ambiguity present. Applying Fourier Transform to imaginary Gaussian (e.g. Proposition 6.2 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wolff, 2003</a>)</cite>), we obtain the following bound for the integral on the right hand side of (<a href="#A7.E76" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix G Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">76</span></a>):</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E77"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E77.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}|\int_{x_{P}}e^{-i\pi\lambda\cdot x_{P}^{\top}\cdot J\cdot x_{P}}\cdot\rho(x_{A},x_{P})dx_{P}|\leq C\lambda^{-(1-\theta)D}\bigg(\sup_{x_{P}}|\rho(x_{A},x_{P})|+\lambda^{-2}\sum_{|\alpha_{P}|=2}\sup_{x_{P}}|D^{\alpha_{P}}\rho(x_{A},x_{P})|\bigg),\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></msub><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi><mi>π</mi><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mi>λ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><mi>λ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>D</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></msup><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}|\int_{x_{P}}e^{-i\pi\lambda\cdot x_{P}^{\top}\cdot J\cdot x_{P}}\cdot\rho(x_{A},x_{P})dx_{P}|\leq C\lambda^{-(1-\theta)D}\bigg(\sup_{x_{P}}|\rho(x_{A},x_{P})|+\lambda^{-2}\sum_{|\alpha_{P}|=2}\sup_{x_{P}}|D^{\alpha_{P}}\rho(x_{A},x_{P})|\bigg),\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(77)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p1.5.1" class="ltx_text">where the summation is taken over all second order derivatives with respect to the <math id="A7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{P}</annotation></semantics></math> variable, and <math id="A7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> is a universal constant. Since <math id="A7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> is in Schwartz class, the following seminorms of <math id="A7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> admit fast decay in <math id="A7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E78"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E78.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\sup_{x_{P}}|\rho(x_{A},x_{P})|,\quad\sup_{x_{P}}|D^{\alpha_{P}}\rho(x_{A},x_{P})|.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></munder><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.889em">,</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\sup_{x_{P}}|\rho(x_{A},x_{P})|,\quad\sup_{x_{P}}|D^{\alpha_{P}}\rho(x_{A},x_{P})|.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(78)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p1.6.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore the following function is integrable in <math id="A7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{A}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{A}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx79" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E79"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E79.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\Phi_{\lambda}(x_{A})\eqqcolon\frac{x_{A}^{\top}\cdot J_{\theta D}\cdot x_{A}}{\sqrt{\theta D}}\cdot\bigg(\sup_{x_{P}}|\rho(x_{A},x_{P})|+\lambda^{-2}\sum_{|\alpha_{P}|=2}\sup_{x_{P}}|D^{\alpha_{P}}\rho(x_{A},x_{P})|\bigg).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≕</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.167em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\Phi_{\lambda}(x_{A})\eqqcolon\frac{x_{A}^{\top}\cdot J_{\theta D}\cdot x_{A}}{\sqrt{\theta D}}\cdot\bigg(\sup_{x_{P}}|\rho(x_{A},x_{P})|+\lambda^{-2}\sum_{|\alpha_{P}|=2}\sup_{x_{P}}|D^{\alpha_{P}}\rho(x_{A},x_{P})|\bigg).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(79)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p1.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p1.7.1" class="ltx_text">Note when <math id="A7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|m-n|\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|m-n|\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, by definition we have <math id="A7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\geq C(D)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\geq C(D)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore <math id="A7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\Phi_{\lambda}\}_{\lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi>λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\Phi_{\lambda}\}_{\lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly bounded in <math id="A7.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{1}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx80" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E80"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E80.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}|\int_{x_{A}}\Phi_{\lambda}(x_{A})dx_{A}|\leq C(\rho,D).\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}|\int_{x_{A}}\Phi_{\lambda}(x_{A})dx_{A}|\leq C(\rho,D).\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(80)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p1.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p1.8.1" class="ltx_text">Combining (<a href="#A7.E75" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix G Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">75</span></a>), (<a href="#A7.E77" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix G Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">77</span></a>), and (<a href="#A7.E80" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix G Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">80</span></a>), we have shown that</span></p>
<table id="A7.EGx81" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A7.E81"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A7.E81.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\Big|\mathbb{E}_{q,k}\text{Attn}_{\theta,\alpha}(q^{(m)},k^{(n)})\Big|\leq C(\rho,D)\lambda^{-(1-\theta)D}=C^{\prime}(\rho,D)|m-n|^{-\alpha(1-\theta)D}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\Big|\mathbb{E}_{q,k}\text{Attn}_{\theta,\alpha}(q^{(m)},k^{(n)})\Big|\leq C(\rho,D)\lambda^{-(1-\theta)D}=C^{\prime}(\rho,D)|m-n|^{-\alpha(1-\theta)D}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(81)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A7.p1.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p1.9.1" class="ltx_text">Thus proves Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Theorem 3.2 (Decaying Bias). ‣ 3 A New Positional Encoding Method: Token-Aware Phase Attention (TAPA) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3 (Long-Context Non-Degeneracy). ‣ 3 A New Positional Encoding Method: Token-Aware Phase Attention (TAPA) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a></h2>

<div id="A8.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">By exploiting the elementary identity <math id="A8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cos^{2}x={(1+\cos 2x)}/{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cos^{2}x={(1+\cos 2x)}/{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we may expand the second moment of Attention as follows:</span></p>
<table id="A8.EGx82" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.E82"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E82.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathbb{E}\Big|\text{Attn}_{\theta,\alpha}\Big|^{2}=&amp;\frac{1}{2}\int_{x_{A}}\frac{(x_{A}^{\top}\cdot J_{\theta D}\cdot x_{A})^{2}}{\theta D}dx_{A}\\
&amp;+\frac{1}{2}\int_{x_{A}}\frac{x_{A}^{\top}\cdot J_{\theta D}\cdot x_{A}}{\sqrt{\theta D}}\bigg(\int_{x_{P}}\cos\Big(\frac{4\pi|m-n|^{\alpha}}{\sqrt{(1-\theta)D}}\cdot x_{P}^{\top}\cdot J_{(1-\theta)D}\cdot x_{P}\Big)\cdot\rho(x_{A},x_{P})dx_{P}\bigg)dx_{A}\\
=&amp;I+II.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><msub><mo>∫</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msub></mstyle><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></msub><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo>∫</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>P</mi></msub></msub><mi>cos</mi><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>J</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.055em">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>P</mi></msub><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mo>=</mo></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}\mathbb{E}\Big|\text{Attn}_{\theta,\alpha}\Big|^{2}=&amp;\frac{1}{2}\int_{x_{A}}\frac{(x_{A}^{\top}\cdot J_{\theta D}\cdot x_{A})^{2}}{\theta D}dx_{A}\\
&amp;+\frac{1}{2}\int_{x_{A}}\frac{x_{A}^{\top}\cdot J_{\theta D}\cdot x_{A}}{\sqrt{\theta D}}\bigg(\int_{x_{P}}\cos\Big(\frac{4\pi|m-n|^{\alpha}}{\sqrt{(1-\theta)D}}\cdot x_{P}^{\top}\cdot J_{(1-\theta)D}\cdot x_{P}\Big)\cdot\rho(x_{A},x_{P})dx_{P}\bigg)dx_{A}\\
=&amp;I+II.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(82)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Notice that</span></p>
<table id="A8.EGx83" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.E83"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E83.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}I=\frac{1}{2\theta D}\mathbb{E}_{q_{A},k_{A}}|q_{A}^{\top}k_{A}|^{2}=\frac{\sigma_{0}^{2}}{2}\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>q</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}I=\frac{1}{2\theta D}\mathbb{E}_{q_{A},k_{A}}|q_{A}^{\top}k_{A}|^{2}=\frac{\sigma_{0}^{2}}{2}\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(83)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">where we used Assumption <a href="#A1.Thmassumption1" title="Assumption A.1. ‣ Appendix A Preparations for proving Theorem , , and ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.1</span></a> in the second identity and <math id="A8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{0}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{0}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined in <a href="#A1.E16" title="In Appendix A Preparations for proving Theorem , , and ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>. Next, we follow an exactly identical argument of estimating <math id="A8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\text{Attn}_{\theta,\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\text{Attn}_{\theta,\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> (see Appendix <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>) to obtain</span></p>
<table id="A8.EGx84" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_eqnarray ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A8.E84"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A8.E84.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\begin{split}|II|\leq C^{\prime\prime}(D,\rho)|m-n|^{-\alpha(1-\theta)D}.\end{split}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>C</mi><mo>′′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\begin{split}|II|\leq C^{\prime\prime}(D,\rho)|m-n|^{-\alpha(1-\theta)D}.\end{split}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(84)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A8.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text">Lastly, combining (<a href="#A7.E81" title="In Proof of Theorem . ‣ Appendix G Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">81</span></a>), (<a href="#A8.E83" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix H Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">83</span></a>), (<a href="#A8.E84" title="In Proof. ‣ Appendix H Proof of Theorem ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">84</span></a>), and taking <math id="A8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\liminf" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>lim inf</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\liminf</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|m-n|\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|m-n|\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math>, we proved (<a href="#S3.E14" title="In Theorem 3.3 (Long-Context Non-Degeneracy). ‣ 3 A New Positional Encoding Method: Token-Aware Phase Attention (TAPA) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>), which concludes Theorem <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem3" title="Theorem 3.3 (Long-Context Non-Degeneracy). ‣ 3 A New Positional Encoding Method: Token-Aware Phase Attention (TAPA) ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Visualize distance bias</h2>

<figure id="A9.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.12635v1/plots/pos_bias_v2.png" id="A9.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:648/197;" width="648" height="197" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span>Empirical distributions of attention score differences, computed over <math id="A9.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10000</annotation></semantics></math> randomly sampled pairs with positions drawn from <math id="A9.F1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,100]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0,100</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,100]</annotation></semantics></math> (short range) and <math id="A9.F1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[10000,10100]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>10000</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10100</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[10000,10100]</annotation></semantics></math> (long range). The skewed distribution of RoPE reflects its strong distance bias, whereas the near-symmetric distribution of TAPA indicates that no significant bias is present.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To visuallize the distance bias of RoPE and TAPA, we compare the distributions of their attention scores difference between short-range and long-range token pairs. More precisely, given two disjoint intervals <math id="A9.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\text{short}}=[0,100]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext>short</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0,100</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\text{short}}=[0,100]</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A9.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I_{\text{long}}=[10000,10100]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext>long</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>10000</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>10100</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I_{\text{long}}=[10000,10100]</annotation></semantics></math>, we randomly sample <math id="A9.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in I_{\text{short}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext>short</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in I_{\text{short}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A9.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\in I_{\text{long}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mtext>long</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\in I_{\text{long}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and compute the difference</p>
<table id="A9.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A9.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta\;=\;\text{Attn}_{\lambda}-\text{Attn}_{\Lambda}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0.558em" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi>λ</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mtext>Attn</mtext><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta\;=\;\text{Attn}_{\lambda}-\text{Attn}_{\Lambda}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A9.p1.2" class="ltx_p">We randomly sample <math id="A9.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10000" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>10000</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10000</annotation></semantics></math> pairs of attention scores satisfying the above positional constraint from the evaluation results on PG19 testset. The resulting histograms (Figure <a href="#A9.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ Appendix I Visualize distance bias ‣ Positional Encoding via Token-Aware Phase Attention" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) show that TAPA produces a highly symmetric distribution centered near zero (<math id="A9.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\approx 0.03,\sigma\approx 3.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.03</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>3.3</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\approx 0.03,\sigma\approx 3.3</annotation></semantics></math>), which indicate low distance bias between near and far token-pairs, while RoPE yields a distribution shifted significantly toward positive values (<math id="A9.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu\approx 4.1,\ \sigma\approx 0.85" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>4.1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>≈</mo><mn>0.85</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu\approx 4.1,\ \sigma\approx 0.85</annotation></semantics></math>), revealing a systematic bias that favors short-range interactions.</p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
</div>
